The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
list_del(&mm->ppgtt_mm.list);
list_del(&mm->ppgtt_mm.lru_list);
```
Reason:
The absence of a mutex lock around the deletion of `lru_list` from `ppgtt_mm` allows multiple threads to access or modify the list concurrently, leading to race conditions that can compromise the integrity of the list, resulting in potential data corruption or crashes.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
mutex_lock(&mm->vgpu->gvt->gtt.ppgtt_mm_lock);
list_del(&mm->ppgtt_mm.lru_list);
mutex_unlock(&mm->vgpu->gvt->gtt.ppgtt_mm_lock);
```
Reason:
By introducing a mutex lock before the deletion of `lru_list` and unlocking it afterward, the code ensures that only one thread can modify the list at a time, thus preventing race conditions and maintaining the integrity of the list during concurrent access.

